# (zname, id, name, latin, synonyms, region, location, description, function, clinical)
C=[]
def a(*t):C.append(t)
# ---- KNEE
a('Medial meniscus','medial-meniscus','Medial meniscus','Meniscus medialis',['knee cartilage'],'lower-limb','Inside the knee joint, between the medial femoral and tibial condyles.','A C-shaped wedge of fibrocartilage that is larger and less mobile than the lateral meniscus and is attached to the medial collateral ligament.','Deepens the tibial surface, spreads load across the joint and helps stabilise the knee.','Tears are common in twisting injuries and with age; a torn meniscus can cause locking, catching and joint-line pain.')
a('Lateral meniscus','lateral-meniscus','Lateral meniscus','Meniscus lateralis',[],'lower-limb','Inside the knee joint, between the lateral femoral and tibial condyles.','A nearly circular fibrocartilage disc that is more mobile than the medial meniscus.','Absorbs shock, spreads load and helps stabilise the knee.','Tears occur with twisting injuries, often together with anterior cruciate ligament injuries.')
a('Transverse ligament of knee','transverse-ligament-of-knee','Transverse ligament of the knee','Ligamentum transversum genus',[],'lower-limb','At the front of the knee, joining the anterior horns of the two menisci.','A thin band of fibres that links the front ends of the medial and lateral menisci.','Ties the two menisci together so they move as a unit.','Rarely injured on its own; it is a landmark on knee imaging and surgery.')
a('Anterior meniscotibial ligament (Lateral meniscus)','meniscotibial-ligaments','Meniscotibial ligaments','Ligamenta meniscotibialia',['coronary ligaments'],'lower-limb','Around the rim of each meniscus, attaching it to the top of the tibia.','Short fibres that anchor the meniscal horns to the tibial plateau.','Hold the menisci in place on the tibia.','Their detachment lets a meniscus move abnormally and can be part of a meniscal root injury.')
a('Posterior meniscotibial ligament (Medial meniscus)','meniscotibial-ligaments',None,None,None,None,None,None,None,None)
a('Deep part of tibial collateral ligament','deep-medial-collateral-ligament','Deep part of the tibial collateral ligament','Pars profunda ligamenti collateralis tibialis',['deep medial collateral ligament'],'lower-limb','Inner side of the knee, deep to the superficial medial collateral ligament.','Short fibres that run from the femur and tibia to the edge of the medial meniscus.','Supports the inner side of the knee and fixes the medial meniscus.','Injury with medial collateral ligament sprains can involve the medial meniscus.')
a('Arcuate popliteal ligament','arcuate-popliteal-ligament','Arcuate popliteal ligament','Ligamentum popliteum arcuatum',[],'lower-limb','Back of the knee, over the popliteus tendon.','A Y-shaped thickening of the posterior capsule arching from the fibular head toward the back of the joint.','Reinforces the back of the knee capsule.','Part of the posterolateral corner of the knee, which is injured in severe knee trauma.')
a('Oblique popliteal ligament','oblique-popliteal-ligament','Oblique popliteal ligament','Ligamentum popliteum obliquum',[],'lower-limb','Back of the knee capsule.','A broad fibrous band that continues from the semimembranosus tendon across the back of the joint.','Reinforces the back of the knee and limits overextension.','Hyperextension injuries can strain it.')
a('Popliteofibular ligament','popliteofibular-ligament','Popliteofibular ligament','Ligamentum popliteofibulare',[],'lower-limb','Back and outer side of the knee.','A band from the popliteus tendon to the head of the fibula.','Stabilises the outer back corner of the knee.','Injured in posterolateral corner injuries, which can cause rotational instability.')
a('Articular capsule of knee joint','knee-joint-capsule','Knee joint capsule','Capsula articularis genus',[],'lower-limb','Surrounds the knee joint.','A fibrous sleeve lined by synovial membrane that encloses the femur, tibia and patella.','Contains the joint fluid and gives passive stability.','Swelling of the capsule (effusion) follows injury, infection and arthritis.')
a('Infrapatellar fat pad','infrapatellar-fat-pad','Infrapatellar fat pad','Corpus adiposum infrapatellare',["Hoffa's fat pad"],'lower-limb','Behind the patellar ligament, below the kneecap.','A pad of fat between the patellar ligament and the front of the knee joint.','Cushions the front of the joint and fills the space as the knee moves.','Can be pinched or inflamed (Hoffa disease), causing pain at the front of the knee.')
# ---- HIP / PELVIS
a('Acetabular labrum','acetabular-labrum','Acetabular labrum','Labrum acetabulare',[],'lower-limb','Rim of the hip socket (acetabulum).','A ring of fibrocartilage that deepens the socket around the femoral head.','Deepens the socket, helps seal the joint and adds stability.','Tears cause groin pain and clicking and are linked to femoroacetabular impingement.')
a('Transverse acetabular ligament','transverse-acetabular-ligament','Transverse acetabular ligament','Ligamentum transversum acetabuli',[],'lower-limb','Across the notch at the bottom of the hip socket.','A strong band that bridges the gap in the acetabular rim.','Completes the ring of the socket and lets vessels pass beneath it to the joint.','A landmark for hip surgery.')
a('Ligament of head of femur','ligament-of-head-of-femur','Ligament of the head of the femur','Ligamentum capitis femoris',['ligamentum teres'],'lower-limb','Inside the hip joint, from the femoral head to the hip socket.','A flat intra-articular band carrying a small artery to the femoral head.','Adds little to stability but carries a small blood supply to the head of the femur.','In adults it can tear; in children its artery is important for the blood supply to the femoral head.')
a('Descending part of iliofemoral ligament','iliofemoral-ligament','Iliofemoral ligament','Ligamentum iliofemorale',['Y-ligament of Bigelow'],'lower-limb','Front of the hip joint.','A Y-shaped ligament, the strongest in the body, running from the pelvis to the front of the femur.','Prevents the hip from over-extending and helps keep the trunk upright when standing.','Tight in standing; it can be torn in severe hip dislocations.')
a('Transverse part of iliofemoral ligament','iliofemoral-ligament',None,None,None,None,None,None,None,None)
a('Pubofemoral ligament','pubofemoral-ligament','Pubofemoral ligament','Ligamentum pubofemorale',[],'lower-limb','Front and underside of the hip joint.','A triangular band from the pubic bone to the neck of the femur.','Limits excessive abduction and extension of the hip.','Part of the capsule that tightens in extreme hip positions.')
a('Ischiofemoral ligament','ischiofemoral-ligament','Ischiofemoral ligament','Ligamentum ischiofemorale',[],'lower-limb','Back of the hip joint.','A spiral band from the ischium to the femoral neck.','Limits internal rotation and extension of the hip.','Contributes to the stability of the back of the hip.')
a('Articular capsule of hip joint','hip-joint-capsule','Hip joint capsule','Capsula articularis coxae',[],'lower-limb','Surrounds the hip joint.','A strong fibrous sleeve reinforced by the iliofemoral, pubofemoral and ischiofemoral ligaments.','Encloses the joint and gives it great stability.','Fractures of the femoral neck inside the capsule can damage the blood supply to the femoral head.')
a('Zona orbicularis','zona-orbicularis','Zona orbicularis','Zona orbicularis',[],'lower-limb','Around the neck of the femur, within the hip capsule.','Circular fibres of the capsule that form a collar around the femoral neck.','Holds the femoral head in the socket like a collar.','Helps resist traction pulling the head out of the socket.')
a('Obturator membrane','obturator-membrane','Obturator membrane','Membrana obturatoria',[],'pelvis','Covers the obturator foramen of the hip bone.','A thin fibrous sheet closing most of the large hole in the hip bone.','Gives attachment to the obturator muscles and leaves a gap for the obturator canal.','The obturator nerve and vessels pass through its canal; obturator hernias can pass there.')
a('Anterior sacro-iliac ligament','anterior-sacro-iliac-ligament','Anterior sacro-iliac ligament','Ligamentum sacroiliacum anterius',[],'pelvis','Front of the sacro-iliac joint.','Flat fibres connecting the sacrum to the ilium at the front of the joint.','Stabilises the sacro-iliac joint and transmits body weight to the pelvis.','Strained in pelvic injuries and in pregnancy-related pelvic pain.')
a('Posterior sacro-iliac ligament','posterior-sacro-iliac-ligament','Posterior sacro-iliac ligament','Ligamentum sacroiliacum posterius',[],'pelvis','Back of the sacro-iliac joint.','Very strong short and long fibres between the sacrum and ilium.','Holds the sacrum into the pelvis and bears the weight of the trunk.','A source of low back and buttock pain when the sacro-iliac joint is irritated.')
a('Sacrotuberous ligament','sacrotuberous-ligament','Sacrotuberous ligament','Ligamentum sacrotuberale',[],'pelvis','Back of the pelvis, from the sacrum to the ischial tuberosity.','A thick fan-shaped band.','Stops the lower sacrum tipping upward and forms part of the pelvic outlet.','The pudendal nerve passes close to it, and it can be involved in pudendal nerve entrapment.')
a('Pubic symphysis','pubic-symphysis','Pubic symphysis','Symphysis pubica',[],'pelvis','At the front of the pelvis, where the two pubic bones meet.','A cartilaginous joint with a fibrocartilage disc between the pubic bones.','Joins the two halves of the pelvis with a little give.','Loosens in pregnancy and can become painful (symphysis pubis dysfunction); it can separate in pelvic trauma.')
a('Interpubic disc','interpubic-disc','Interpubic disc','Discus interpubicus',[],'pelvis','Inside the pubic symphysis.','A plate of fibrocartilage between the two pubic bones.','Absorbs load and allows slight movement at the pubic symphysis.','Widens in late pregnancy.')
a('Sacrococcygeal symphysis','sacrococcygeal-symphysis','Sacrococcygeal symphysis','Symphysis sacrococcygea',[],'pelvis','Between the lower end of the sacrum and the coccyx.','A cartilaginous joint with a small fibrocartilage disc.','Lets the coccyx move slightly, for example in childbirth.','Can be painful after a fall (coccydynia).')
# ---- SHOULDER / ELBOW
a('Glenoid labrum','glenoid-labrum','Glenoid labrum','Labrum glenoidale',[],'upper-limb','Rim of the shoulder socket (glenoid cavity).','A ring of fibrocartilage around the edge of the glenoid.','Deepens the shallow shoulder socket and helps keep the humeral head in place.','Tears (such as Bankart and SLAP lesions) occur with shoulder dislocation and overhead throwing.')
a('Middle glenohumeral ligament','middle-glenohumeral-ligament','Middle glenohumeral ligament','Ligamentum glenohumerale medium',[],'upper-limb','Front of the shoulder joint capsule.','A band thickening the front of the capsule below the subscapularis tendon.','Limits external rotation of the arm at mid-range elevation.','Variable in size; injured in anterior shoulder dislocations.')
a('Inferior glenohumeral ligament','inferior-glenohumeral-ligament','Inferior glenohumeral ligament','Ligamentum glenohumerale inferius',[],'upper-limb','Lower part of the shoulder joint capsule.','A hammock-like band with anterior and posterior parts.','The main restraint against the humeral head slipping out when the arm is raised and rotated.','Stretched or torn in recurrent shoulder dislocation.')
a('Articular capsule of glenohumeral joint','glenohumeral-joint-capsule','Glenohumeral joint capsule','Capsula articularis glenohumeralis',['shoulder joint capsule'],'upper-limb','Surrounds the shoulder joint.','A loose fibrous sleeve from the glenoid to the neck of the humerus, reinforced by the rotator cuff and glenohumeral ligaments.','Encloses the joint and permits a wide range of movement.','Becomes thickened and stiff in adhesive capsulitis (frozen shoulder).')
a('Articular capsule of acromioclavicular joint','acromioclavicular-joint-capsule','Acromioclavicular joint capsule','Capsula articularis acromioclavicularis',[],'upper-limb','Top of the shoulder, between the collarbone and the acromion.','A thin capsule strengthened by the acromioclavicular ligaments.','Holds the outer end of the clavicle to the acromion.','Injured in falls onto the point of the shoulder (AC joint sprain or separation).')
a('Articular capsule of sternoclavicular joint','sternoclavicular-joint-capsule','Sternoclavicular joint capsule','Capsula articularis sternoclavicularis',[],'thorax','Where the collarbone meets the breastbone.','A strong capsule reinforced by the sternoclavicular ligaments.','The only bony joint between the arm and the trunk skeleton; it holds the clavicle to the sternum.','Dislocations are rare but dangerous when the clavicle moves behind the sternum.')
a('Annular ligament of radius','annular-ligament-of-radius','Annular ligament of the radius','Ligamentum anulare radii',[],'upper-limb','Around the head of the radius at the elbow.','A fibrous ring that wraps the radial head against the ulna.','Holds the radial head in place while the forearm rotates.','Children can pull the radial head out of it ("pulled elbow", nursemaid elbow).')
a('Articular capsule of elbow joint','elbow-joint-capsule','Elbow joint capsule','Capsula articularis cubiti',[],'upper-limb','Surrounds the elbow joint.','A thin fibrous sleeve around the humero-ulnar, humeroradial and radio-ulnar joints.','Encloses the elbow and, with the collateral ligaments, keeps it stable.','Swells with elbow injury, infection or arthritis.')
# ---- WRIST / HAND
a('Articular capsule of radiocarpal joint','radiocarpal-joint-capsule','Radiocarpal joint capsule','Capsula articularis radiocarpalis',['wrist joint capsule'],'upper-limb','Surrounds the wrist joint.','A fibrous capsule between the radius and the proximal carpal bones.','Encloses the wrist joint.','Ganglion cysts often arise from it.')
a('Dorsal radiocarpal ligament','dorsal-radiocarpal-ligament','Dorsal radiocarpal ligament','Ligamentum radiocarpale dorsale',[],'upper-limb','Back of the wrist.','A band from the radius to the carpal bones on the dorsal side.','Stabilises the back of the wrist and limits flexion.','Strained in wrist hyperflexion injuries.')
a('Radiate carpal ligament','radiate-carpal-ligament','Radiate carpal ligament','Ligamentum carpi radiatum',[],'upper-limb','Palm side of the wrist.','Fibres radiating from the capitate to neighbouring carpal bones.','Binds the carpal bones together on the palm side.','Part of the ligament complex involved in carpal instability.')
a('Pisotriquetral ligament','pisotriquetral-ligament','Pisotriquetral ligament','Ligamentum pisotriquetrum',[],'upper-limb','Inner wrist, between the pisiform and triquetrum.','A short band joining the two bones.','Holds the pisiform to the triquetrum.','Pisotriquetral joint arthritis can cause pain at the inner wrist.')
a('Dorsal intercarpal ligaments','dorsal-intercarpal-ligaments','Dorsal intercarpal ligaments','Ligamenta intercarpalia dorsalia',[],'upper-limb','Back of the carpus.','Short bands linking neighbouring carpal bones.','Hold the carpal bones together.','Injury can lead to carpal instability.')
a('Dorsal carpometacarpal ligaments','dorsal-carpometacarpal-ligaments','Dorsal carpometacarpal ligaments','Ligamenta carpometacarpalia dorsalia',[],'upper-limb','Back of the hand, at the base of the metacarpals.','Bands from the distal carpal bones to the metacarpal bases.','Stabilise the carpometacarpal joints.','Strained in falls onto the hand.')
a('Palmar carpometacarpal ligaments','palmar-carpometacarpal-ligaments','Palmar carpometacarpal ligaments','Ligamenta carpometacarpalia palmaria',[],'upper-limb','Palm side at the base of the metacarpals.','Bands from the distal carpal bones to the metacarpal bases.','Stabilise the carpometacarpal joints on the palm side.','Support the arch of the hand.')
a('Articular capsules of metacarpophalangeal joints','metacarpophalangeal-joint-capsules','Metacarpophalangeal joint capsules','Capsulae articulares metacarpophalangeae',['knuckle joint capsules'],'upper-limb','Around the knuckle joints of the hand.','Fibrous capsules around each metacarpophalangeal joint.','Enclose the knuckle joints.','Commonly inflamed in rheumatoid arthritis.')
a('Collateral metacarpophalangeal ligaments','collateral-metacarpophalangeal-ligaments','Collateral metacarpophalangeal ligaments','Ligamenta collateralia articulationum metacarpophalangealium',[],'upper-limb','Sides of the knuckle joints.','Cord-like bands on each side of the metacarpophalangeal joints.','Stabilise the knuckle against sideways force.','The thumb one is injured in "skier\'s thumb".')
a('Articular capsules of proximal interphalangeal joints','proximal-interphalangeal-joint-capsules-hand','Proximal interphalangeal joint capsules (hand)','Capsulae articulares interphalangeae proximales manus',['PIP joint capsules'],'upper-limb','Around the middle finger joints.','Fibrous capsules of the finger joints nearest the knuckle.','Enclose the PIP joints.','Dislocations and "jammed finger" injuries involve these joints.')
a('Articular capsules of distal interphalangeal joints','distal-interphalangeal-joint-capsules-hand','Distal interphalangeal joint capsules (hand)','Capsulae articulares interphalangeae distales manus',['DIP joint capsules'],'upper-limb','Around the finger-tip joints.','Fibrous capsules of the last finger joints.','Enclose the DIP joints.','Heberden nodes of osteoarthritis form at these joints.')
a('Collateral interphalangeal ligaments of hand','collateral-interphalangeal-ligaments-hand','Collateral interphalangeal ligaments (hand)','Ligamenta collateralia articulationum interphalangealium manus',[],'upper-limb','Sides of the finger joints.','Cord-like ligaments on each side of the finger joints.','Prevent sideways bending of the fingers.','Sprained in sports injuries.')
a('Palmar interphalangeal ligaments','palmar-interphalangeal-ligaments','Palmar interphalangeal ligaments','Ligamenta palmaria articulationum interphalangealium',['volar plates'],'upper-limb','Palm side of the finger joints.','Thick fibrocartilage plates on the palm side of each finger joint.','Prevent the finger joints from bending backward (hyperextension).','Torn in hyperextension injuries of the fingers.')
# ---- FOOT / ANKLE
a('Anterior tibiofibular ligament','anterior-tibiofibular-ligament','Anterior tibiofibular ligament','Ligamentum tibiofibulare anterius',[],'lower-limb','Front of the ankle, between the tibia and fibula.','A band joining the lower ends of the tibia and fibula in front.','Holds the ankle mortise together.','Torn in high ankle sprains.')
a('Posterior tibiofibular ligament','posterior-tibiofibular-ligament','Posterior tibiofibular ligament','Ligamentum tibiofibulare posterius',[],'lower-limb','Back of the ankle, between the tibia and fibula.','A strong band joining the lower ends of the tibia and fibula behind.','Holds the ankle mortise together.','Injured in syndesmosis (high ankle) injuries.')
a('Articular capsule of superior tibiofibular joint','superior-tibiofibular-joint-capsule','Superior tibiofibular joint capsule','Capsula articularis tibiofibularis',[],'lower-limb','Below the knee, where the fibular head meets the tibia.','A capsule around the joint between the head of the fibula and the tibia.','Encloses the superior tibiofibular joint.','Dislocation is uncommon and follows twisting injuries.')
a('Tibionavicular ligament','tibionavicular-ligament','Tibionavicular ligament','Ligamentum tibionaviculare',[],'lower-limb','Inner side of the ankle.','A band of the deltoid ligament running from the medial malleolus to the navicular.','Supports the inner side of the ankle.','Part of the deltoid ligament, injured in eversion ankle sprains.')
a('Talocalcaneal interosseous ligament','talocalcaneal-interosseous-ligament','Talocalcaneal interosseous ligament','Ligamentum talocalcaneum interosseum',[],'lower-limb','Deep in the sinus tarsi, between the talus and heel bone.','A strong band joining the talus and calcaneus.','Binds the talus to the calcaneus and stabilises the subtalar joint.','Sprained in inversion injuries and can cause sinus tarsi pain.')
a('Dorsal tarsometatarsal ligaments','dorsal-tarsometatarsal-ligaments','Dorsal tarsometatarsal ligaments','Ligamenta tarsometatarsalia dorsalia',[],'lower-limb','Top of the midfoot.','Bands joining the tarsal bones to the metatarsal bases.','Stabilise the midfoot joints.','Disrupted in Lisfranc injuries.')
a('Plantar tarsometatarsal ligaments','plantar-tarsometatarsal-ligaments','Plantar tarsometatarsal ligaments','Ligamenta tarsometatarsalia plantaria',[],'lower-limb','Sole of the midfoot.','Bands joining the tarsal bones to the metatarsal bases on the sole side.','Support the arches of the foot.','Involved in Lisfranc injuries.')
a('Articular capsules of metatarsophalangeal joints','metatarsophalangeal-joint-capsules','Metatarsophalangeal joint capsules','Capsulae articulares metatarsophalangeae',[],'lower-limb','Around the ball-of-the-foot joints.','Fibrous capsules around each metatarsophalangeal joint.','Enclose the joints at the base of the toes.','The great toe joint is a common site of gout and bunions.')
a('Collateral metatarsophalangeal ligaments','collateral-metatarsophalangeal-ligaments','Collateral metatarsophalangeal ligaments','Ligamenta collateralia articulationum metatarsophalangealium',[],'lower-limb','Sides of the metatarsophalangeal joints.','Cord-like bands on each side of the joints.','Stabilise the toe joints against sideways force.','Sprained in "turf toe" type injuries.')
a('Plantar metatarsophalangeal ligaments','plantar-metatarsophalangeal-ligaments','Plantar metatarsophalangeal ligaments','Ligamenta plantaria articulationum metatarsophalangealium',['plantar plates'],'lower-limb','Sole side of the toe joints.','Thick fibrocartilage plates under each joint.','Protect the joint on the sole side and resist hyperextension.','Tears cause forefoot pain and toe deformities.')
a('Articular capsules of proximal interphalangeal joints of foot','proximal-interphalangeal-joint-capsules-foot','Proximal interphalangeal joint capsules (foot)','Capsulae articulares interphalangeae proximales pedis',[],'lower-limb','Around the middle toe joints.','Fibrous capsules of the toe joints.','Enclose the PIP joints of the toes.','Involved in hammer toe deformities.')
a('Articular capsules of distal interphalangeal joints of foot','distal-interphalangeal-joint-capsules-foot','Distal interphalangeal joint capsules (foot)','Capsulae articulares interphalangeae distales pedis',[],'lower-limb','Around the end toe joints.','Fibrous capsules of the last toe joints.','Enclose the DIP joints of the toes.','Involved in mallet toe deformities.')
a('Articular capsule of interphalangeal joint of great toe','great-toe-interphalangeal-joint-capsule','Great toe interphalangeal joint capsule','Capsula articularis interphalangea hallucis',[],'lower-limb','Around the joint of the big toe.','A fibrous capsule around the single joint of the big toe.','Encloses the interphalangeal joint of the great toe.','Can be injured by stubbing the toe.')
a('Collateral interphalangeal ligaments of foot','collateral-interphalangeal-ligaments-foot','Collateral interphalangeal ligaments (foot)','Ligamenta collateralia articulationum interphalangealium pedis',[],'lower-limb','Sides of the toe joints.','Cord-like ligaments at the sides of the toe joints.','Stabilise the toes against sideways force.','Sprained when toes are jammed.')
a('Plantar interphalangeal ligaments','plantar-interphalangeal-ligaments','Plantar interphalangeal ligaments','Ligamenta plantaria articulationum interphalangealium pedis',[],'lower-limb','Sole side of the toe joints.','Plates of fibrocartilage on the underside of the toe joints.','Resist bending the toes upward too far.','Injured in hyperextension of the toes.')
# ---- SPINE
a('Anterior longitudinal ligament','anterior-longitudinal-ligament','Anterior longitudinal ligament','Ligamentum longitudinale anterius',[],'back','Down the front of the vertebral bodies, from skull base to sacrum.','A strong, wide band attached to the fronts of the vertebrae and discs.','Limits backward bending of the spine and supports the front of the discs.','Torn in whiplash hyperextension injuries.')
a('Posterior longitudinal ligament','posterior-longitudinal-ligament','Posterior longitudinal ligament','Ligamentum longitudinale posterius',[],'back','Down the back of the vertebral bodies, inside the spinal canal.','A narrower band that runs from the axis to the sacrum along the floor of the canal.','Limits forward bending of the spine and helps stop discs bulging backward.','Disc herniation often tracks to the side of it; ossification can narrow the canal.')
a('Ligamenta flava','ligamenta-flava','Ligamenta flava','Ligamenta flava',['yellow ligaments'],'back','Between the laminae of adjacent vertebrae, inside the spinal canal.','Elastic yellow ligaments joining each lamina to the next.','Help the spine return upright after bending and protect the spinal cord.','They thicken with age and can narrow the canal (spinal stenosis); a needle passes through them in epidural injection.')
a('Interspinous ligaments','interspinous-ligaments','Interspinous ligaments','Ligamenta interspinalia',[],'back','Between adjacent spinous processes.','Thin bands joining the spinous processes of neighbouring vertebrae.','Limit over-bending forward.','Sprained in flexion injuries.')
a('Supraspinous ligament','supraspinous-ligament','Supraspinous ligament','Ligamentum supraspinale',[],'back','Along the tips of the spinous processes.','A band running over the tips of the spinous processes.','Limits forward bending of the spine.','Can be strained in back injuries; in the neck it continues as the nuchal ligament.')
a('Nuchal ligament','nuchal-ligament','Nuchal ligament','Ligamentum nuchae',[],'neck','Back of the neck, from the skull to C7.','A thick sheet of fibres continuing the supraspinous ligament upward.','Supports the head and gives attachment to neck muscles.','Strained in neck flexion injuries.')
a('Intertransverse ligaments','intertransverse-ligaments','Intertransverse ligaments','Ligamenta intertransversaria',[],'back','Between adjacent transverse processes.','Small bands connecting neighbouring transverse processes.','Limit bending of the spine to the opposite side.','Minor stabilisers of the spine.')
# ---- RIBS
a('Costotransverse ligament','costotransverse-ligament','Costotransverse ligament','Ligamentum costotransversarium',[],'thorax','Between a rib neck and the transverse process of its vertebra.','A short band at each costotransverse joint.','Holds the rib to the vertebra.','Part of the rib-spine joints that can be painful in back strain.')
a('Radiate ligament of head of rib','radiate-ligament-of-head-of-rib','Radiate ligament of the head of the rib','Ligamentum capitis costae radiatum',[],'thorax','Front of the joint between a rib head and the vertebral bodies.','A fan-shaped band from the rib head to the vertebrae and the disc between them.','Secures the rib head to the spine.','Can be a source of pain in rib-vertebral joint dysfunction.')
a('Intra-articular ligament of head of rib','intra-articular-ligament-of-head-of-rib','Intra-articular ligament of the head of the rib','Ligamentum capitis costae intraarticulare',[],'thorax','Inside the joint of the rib head.','A short band from the rib head to the intervertebral disc.','Divides the joint into two compartments and holds the rib head.','Part of the rib-spine connection.')
a('External intercostal membrane','external-intercostal-membrane','External intercostal membrane','Membrana intercostalis externa',[],'thorax','Between the ribs near the breastbone, over the internal intercostal muscles.','A thin fibrous sheet filling the space between the ribs at the front.','Takes the place of the external intercostal muscle near the sternum.','Not clinically significant on its own.')
a('Internal intercostal membrane','internal-intercostal-membrane','Internal intercostal membrane','Membrana intercostalis interna',[],'thorax','Between the ribs near the spine.','A thin fibrous sheet filling the space between the ribs at the back.','Takes the place of the internal intercostal muscle near the spine.','Not clinically significant on its own.')
# ---- HEAD/NECK
a('Lateral temporomandibular ligament','lateral-temporomandibular-ligament','Lateral temporomandibular ligament','Ligamentum laterale articulationis temporomandibularis',[],'head','Outer side of the jaw joint.','A band reinforcing the outside of the capsule from the zygomatic arch to the mandible.','Limits backward movement of the lower jaw.','Overstretched in jaw dislocation.')
a('Sphenomandibular ligament','sphenomandibular-ligament','Sphenomandibular ligament','Ligamentum sphenomandibulare',[],'head','Inner side of the jaw joint.','A flat band from the sphenoid spine to the lingula of the mandible.','Suspends the lower jaw from the skull.','The inferior alveolar nerve passes close to it, which matters for nerve blocks.')
a('Stylohyoid ligament','stylohyoid-ligament','Stylohyoid ligament','Ligamentum stylohyoideum',[],'neck','From the styloid process to the hyoid bone.','A fibrous cord that can partly ossify.','Suspends the hyoid bone from the skull base.','An ossified or elongated one can cause throat pain in Eagle syndrome.')
a('Cricopharyngeal ligament','cricopharyngeal-ligament','Cricopharyngeal ligament','Ligamentum cricopharyngeum',[],'neck','Back of the larynx, from the cricoid to the pharynx.','A band connecting the cricoid cartilage to the arytenoid and pharynx.','Anchors the pharynx to the back of the larynx.','Related to the area where pharyngeal pouches form.')
a('Lateral thyrohyoid ligament','lateral-thyrohyoid-ligament','Lateral thyrohyoid ligament','Ligamentum thyrohyoideum laterale',[],'neck','Side of the larynx, from the thyroid cartilage to the hyoid.','A cord at each free edge of the thyrohyoid membrane.','Connects the larynx to the hyoid bone.','Surgical landmark.')
a('Median thyrohyoid ligament','median-thyrohyoid-ligament','Median thyrohyoid ligament','Ligamentum thyrohyoideum medianum',[],'neck','Front of the neck, between the hyoid and thyroid cartilage.','The thickened centre of the thyrohyoid membrane.','Joins the thyroid cartilage to the hyoid bone and lets the larynx rise when swallowing.','A landmark in neck surgery.')
a('Median cricothyroid ligament','median-cricothyroid-ligament','Median cricothyroid ligament','Ligamentum cricothyroideum medianum',['cricothyroid membrane'],'neck','Front of the neck, between the thyroid and cricoid cartilages.','A strong triangular band beneath the skin.','Joins the thyroid and cricoid cartilages.','The site for an emergency airway (cricothyrotomy).')
a('Quadrangular membrane','quadrangular-membrane','Quadrangular membrane','Membrana quadrangularis',[],'neck','Inside the larynx, above the vocal folds.','A sheet of fibres running between the epiglottis and the arytenoid cartilages.','Forms the framework of the vestibular (false) folds.','Part of the supraglottic larynx.')
